%H A401663 Scott R. Shannon, <a href="/A401663/a401663_9.jpg">Image for n = 45</a>. The 45th circle is only ~0.01770 radians from the 1st circle.
%H A401663 Scott R. Shannon, <a href="/A401663/a401663_10.jpg">Image for n = 48</a>. The trailing edge of the 48th circle is very close to the leading edges of the 1st and 45th circles, just right of the 12 o-clock position near the origin. These intersections create a new 2-sided region, breaking the run of constant 2-sided region count, and starts a range of n values where the number of 2-sided regions increases while the number of 3-sided regions decreases.
%F A401663 Total number of regions = n*(n+1)/2, n >= 1.
%F A401663 Total number of vertices = n*(n-1)/2 + 1, n >= 2.
%F A401663 Total number of edges = n^2, n >= 1.
